\subsection{Scanning and Detection}

The scanner module orchestrates Nmap as an external child process. A two-phase progressive scan design was adopted to balance the competing demands of responsiveness and coverage identified in the detection literature~\cite{chalvatzis2019}: Phase 1 scans the top 100 ports and returns early results to the user within approximately two to four minutes, while Phase 2 runs a full 65,535-port scan in the background. The results are merged with deduplication after both phases complete. The parser additionally injects post-processing detections for missing security headers and absent HTTPS, extending coverage into configuration-level findings that Nmap's scripting engine does not natively report. Figure \ref{fig:scan-target} shows the scan target interface with allowlist validation confirmed and the six-step progress stepper prior to execution.

