\section{Summary}
This chapter has established the methodological foundation for the evaluation that follows. The system was designed against seven traceable requirements derived from the proposal objectives, each mapped to a specific pipeline module and a defined evaluation phase. The pipeline architecture separates discovery, deterministic analysis and AI enrichment into independently testable modules, with a runtime feature toggle system enabling controlled ablation of individual components without modifying the codebase. The evaluation framework comprises five phases covering baseline consistency, exploitability-aware scoring impact, per-feature contribution isolation, iterative lifecycle demonstration and longitudinal hallucination reliability. All testing is restricted to authorised targets under the ethical constraints described in Section 3.4, and the evaluation metrics are drawn directly from the literature-established constraints reviewed in Chapter 2. The system is feature-complete, and the results of executing this evaluation framework are presented in Chapter 4.

