distinguishes between resolved and persisting findings across consecutive scan
cycles, which is the core requirement of the lifecycle tracking capability
described in Section~\ref{sec:system-design}.

The 57-point score improvement also validates the scoring engine's sensitivity
to remediation activity, since the removal of higher-severity findings produced
a proportionally larger score recovery than the removal of Informational entries
alone would have achieved. The fact that the post-remediation score reached 60
rather than a substantially higher value reflects the continued presence of 1
High and 1 Medium finding in the residual vulnerability set, which is a
constraint that demonstrates the scoring engine penalising persisting
high-severity findings as designed. Taken together, these results confirm that
the scan-remediate-rescan lifecycle operates as intended, producing traceable
delta outputs that an operator could use to measure remediation progress across
iterative assessment cycles.

