PurpleTeam Suite is the only tool in the comparison that implements a closed-loop
pipeline from network-layer scanning through AI-enriched classification, deterministic
hallucination validation, contextual scoring and iterative lifecycle comparison within
a single desktop application. Splunk SOAR comes closest in terms of AI-assisted
remediation and iterative delta tracking, but it operates as an orchestration layer
over existing scanners rather than providing integrated scanning, and it carries a
commercial licence cost. Nessus provides strong scanning breadth and reporting but
lacks contextual weighting, hallucination validation, and open-source availability.
The scanning tools (Nmap, OWASP ZAP, OpenVAS, Burp Suite) each cover detection
within their respective layers but would require manual integration or third-party
orchestration to achieve equivalent lifecycle coverage. The comparison should be
interpreted with the caveat noted in Section~\ref{sec:limitations-ethics}:
PurpleTeam Suite relies on Nmap as its sole scanner, which restricts detection to
the network layer, whereas OWASP ZAP and Burp Suite operate at the application
layer and can identify vulnerability classes that network-level scanning cannot reach.

