\section{Summary}
\label{sec:ch4-summary}

The five-phase evaluation produced quantitative evidence across all pipeline
components: Phase~1 established deterministic baseline scores ranging from 50 to
181 severity deductions across five targets, Phase~2 demonstrated a 69.2\%
amplification from contextual weighting on the Mutillidae target, and Phase~3
confirmed contextual weighting as the highest-impact component with a 74-point
ablation delta. Phase~4 validated the lifecycle tracking system with a 57-point
score improvement and 53\% vulnerability reduction on the controlled testbed,
while Phase~5 recorded zero fabricated CVEs across all 11 scans and identified
trust score variation as a function of target complexity rather than a systematic
guard deficiency. These results, taken together with the limitations identified
in Section~\ref{sec:eval-limitations}, provide the empirical basis for the
conclusions and recommendations presented in Chapter~5.


